From 31c8ff6b5827f9c24e387b18329e1a541412c632 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:26:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ioRTCW-PS3 1.1: vertex work on the RSX (r_ps3_vprog)

From IoQuake3-PS3's November 2026 "RSX changes" (Mayo1970), adapted to the
iortcw renderer:

- q3_vp_gen, a second vertex program (cgc from q3_vp_gen.vcg, kept as
  NV40 assembly in shaders/asm), computes stage colors, texcoords (env,
  vector, tcMods incl. RTCW's swap), model diffuse lighting and the
  wave/bulge/move deforms on the RSX, with the same GL fog as q3_vp.
- tr_ps3_vprog.c folds a stage into its uniforms in place of
  ComputeColors/ComputeTexCoords/RB_CalcDiffuseColor/RB_DeformTessGeometry;
  whatever the VP can't reproduce (normalzfade, firerise env, fading
  models, fire-rise deforms, fog-adjusted colors, greyscale) stays on the
  PPU as in 1.0.
- ps3gl: per-draw uniforms uploaded only when they change, the stages of a
  surface reuse the first stage's vertex copy and converted indices,
  normals bound on ATTR2 when the VP needs them.
- r_ps3_vprog 0 brings back 1.0's path; DIAG builds log the stage draws
  that went to the RSX. Version 1.1, patch 20.

